WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.060
For many, becoming an actor is the ultimate dream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.026
job. But most of these performers&nbsp;
had their sights set elsewhere.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.640
"School of Rock" was a film that helped prove&nbsp;
Jack Black was more than just a gimmick. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.960
had appeared in movies before and found plenty&nbsp;
of success with his musical group Tenacious D,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.940
but this was the flick that helped transform&nbsp;
him into a household name. What truly makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.260
him shine in "School of Rock" is the way he&nbsp;
works with his reluctant bandmates. And of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.520
that group of students, there are few kids as&nbsp;
memorable as Lawrence, the keyboard maestro.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.360
Played by Robert Tsai, Lawrence is one of&nbsp;
the most skilled performers in the band,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.668
but his insecurities nearly&nbsp;
derail his opportunities.

00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:38.655
"I don't think I should be in the band."&nbsp;

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.920
"Why not?"
"I'm not cool enough."

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.280
According to "School of Rock"&nbsp;
director Richard Linklater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.020
he drew on a real interaction with Robert&nbsp;
Tsai for Lawrence's emotional scene. Tsai&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.100
apparently tried to quit the film, telling&nbsp;
Linklater that he thought he was unfit for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.480
the role. The director convinced him to stay&nbsp;
and reworked that conversation into a scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.960
where Lawrence expresses concern that&nbsp;
he's not cool enough to be in the band.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.480
Tsai never acted again after "School of Rock," but&nbsp;
he continues to perform as a classical pianist.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.100
For a bit of childhood wonder, look no further&nbsp;
than "Willy Wonka &amp; the Chocolate Factory."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:17.160
The 1971 movie is remembered for many things,&nbsp;
including Gene Wilder's iconic purple-suited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:23.640
chocolatier, a number of deceptive traps, some&nbsp;
very ominous songs, and the blue-eyed hero of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.500
all — Charlie Bucket. Played by Peter Ostrum,&nbsp;
Charlie proves his selflessness to Wonka and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.880
wins the day, sparking hope for his destitute&nbsp;
family when he is awarded Wonka's factory.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.340
Ostrum told the Journal of the American Veterinary&nbsp;
Medical Association that after playing the role of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.900
Charlie, he was offered a three-film deal by&nbsp;
the studio if he signed with them. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.740
he declined in order to keep his options&nbsp;
open and give himself more freedom.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.540
Though he did audition for a few more roles as&nbsp;
he got older, Ostrum was drawn to the world of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.220
veterinary medicine. He eventually moved to New&nbsp;
York and claims he'd distanced himself from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.140
movie, rarely telling people about that part of&nbsp;
his life. But as he's grown older, he's embraced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.460
that aspect of his history, especially the&nbsp;
mentoring relationship he had with Wilder.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.980
Steven Spielberg's "Hook" is fondly remembered&nbsp;
for its incredible cast and fun reimagining of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.480
the classic "Peter Pan" story. Who can forget&nbsp;
Dustin Hoffman's scenery-chewing Captain Hook&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.400
performance or Robin Williams' Peter Pan and his&nbsp;
playful banter with Julia Roberts' Tinker Bell?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.700
The boo box? Run home Jack? Ru-fi-ohhh? We're&nbsp;
talking about a stone-cold classic right here.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.240
"Looky looky, I got hooky"

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:35.340
Often lost in the shuffle is Peter's daughter,&nbsp;
Maggie. Played by then-seven-year-old Amber Scott,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:40.140
Maggie has scene-stealing moments throughout&nbsp;
the film. But despite her terrific performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.020
Scott's only other acting&nbsp;
credit is as a voice actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.960
on the historical documentary&nbsp;
series "American Experience."

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:51.300
Scott seemingly went on to a normal life as&nbsp;
she grew older, attending Trinity College and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.580
getting her degree. She eventually updated her&nbsp;
headshot on IMDb and received a producer credit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.780
for the short film "Cannonball." Maybe she's&nbsp;
still gearing up for a return to Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.709
but we haven't heard anything&nbsp;
in a few years from her camp.

00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:07.740
There are only a handful of films that&nbsp;
commonly get mentioned in debates over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:13.800
the best sci-fi movies of all time, but "Aliens"&nbsp;
is generally on the shortlist. Released in 1986,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.520
it leans hard into its high-octane&nbsp;
action to tell an entirely different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.420
story than its predecessor — one that&nbsp;
still holds up as a classic today.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.340
"Aliens" is largely successful because of the&nbsp;
very relatable relationship between Ripley and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:31.200
Newt — the scared little girl she protects from&nbsp;
the xenomorph menace. Played by Carrie Henn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.800
Newt gives the audience a surrogate&nbsp;
character who is just as terrified in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.420
the face of an interstellar monster as we would&nbsp;
be, fighting to stay alive against all the odds.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:44.460
Despite her strong performance, the timing just&nbsp;
didn't work out for Henn. After "Aliens" was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:49.080
released, her family had already moved from&nbsp;
London to the United States. She told Wired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.880
that she had grown more interested in becoming an&nbsp;
educator than an actor, leading her to a career as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:59.100
an elementary teacher. Even so, Henn embraces her&nbsp;
legendary role; you can catch her at conventions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:03.069
and she is happy to sign autographs for&nbsp;
her students when they realize who she is.

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:07.920
The American road movie's poster child is "Easy&nbsp;
Rider," but there’s a number of films that fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.660
the category. One that often flies under the&nbsp;
radar is "Two-Lane Blacktop" — a minimalistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:18.240
film about a duo of road racers who flit across&nbsp;
the country in their Chevy 150. Singer-songwriter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.320
James Taylor and Beach Boys drummer Dennis&nbsp;
Wilson play the lead roles. And while Taylor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.022 --> 00:04:26.760
has since done sporadic acting in his career,&nbsp;
Wilson only made this one appearance on film.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.200
Wilson may have been primed for a successful&nbsp;
career as both a musician and an actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.880
but one unlucky encounter seemed to derail&nbsp;
his life. The Beach Boys drummer had a habit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.960
of picking up hitchhikers, and one day he&nbsp;
brought two young women back to his home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.980
After leaving for a recording session,&nbsp;
he came back to his house to discover the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:48.180
women had invited even more people over.&nbsp;
One of them was a young Charles Manson.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.920
As Wilson's life was slowly eroded by&nbsp;
Manson and his cult, he turned to heavy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:58.189
substance abuse. He died at the age of 39,&nbsp;
drowning after diving into Marina Del Rey.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:03.180
Though not as impactful as "The Omen," the&nbsp;
sequel is vastly superior to the third and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.920
fourth entries in the franchise. And we&nbsp;
don't even bother with the 2006 remake.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:12.480
In "Damien: Omen II," everyone's favorite&nbsp;
antichrist is a preteen living with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:17.220
uncle in Chicago and attending a military&nbsp;
academy. The only semblance of a true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.140
friend he has is his cousin Mark, played&nbsp;
by Lucas Donat. When Mark learns Damien's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:26.520
true nature and confronts him, Damien gives&nbsp;
him the chance to join him. Mark refuses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.520
and Damien kills his cousin in&nbsp;
order to protect his secret.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.780
After leaving the acting profession,&nbsp;
Donat became a prolific advertising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:38.460
executive for Tiny Rebellion — a firm&nbsp;
that won the 2014 Small Agency Award&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:42.540
from AdAge. Donat has been praised for&nbsp;
his disruptive approach and for helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:47.480
to spearhead the marketing campaigns for&nbsp;
companies like LegalZoom and eHarmony.

